      "updated": 1790918156860,
      "created": 1790914860344,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "As of now I'm thinking I can\nstore the rules purely in Java,\nbut I think that is not scalable\nwhen there are so many rules. \nShould I create a class called\nPolicy and PolicyFactory that\nwould give me the correct rule ? ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "9zDpjR1v5XHYWmCypNCTX",
      "originalText": "As of now I'm thinking I can store the rules purely in Java, but I think that is not scalable when there are so many rules. \nShould I create a class called Policy and PolicyFactory that would give me the correct rule ? ",
